<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/15th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Bô Cô</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1408">1408</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> · Also known as Battle of Bo Co</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Bô Cô was fought in late 1408 in what is now <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nam-dinh">Nam Định</a> province, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vietnam">Vietnam</a>, between the Later Tran forces of Emperor Gian Dinh and a Ming army under Mu Sheng. The Vietnamese, led by the generals <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dang-tat">Dang Tat</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nguyen-canh-chan">Nguyen Canh Chan</a>, won a major victory, killing the Ming minister <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emperor-xiaowu-of-liu-song">Liu Jun</a>. Gian Dinh failed to follow it up and soon had both generals executed.</p></div>
